[manpage_begin nsstats n 1.15]
[moddesc {NaviServer External Modules}]
[titledesc {Monitoring and statistics web interface}]
[description]
The nsstats module provides an administrative web interface for NaviServer.
It displays process information, virtual-server configuration, connection pools,
network drivers, background jobs, memory, caches, shared variables and logs.
Features are detected at runtime so older supported NaviServer releases remain usable.

[section INSTALLATION]
Place [file nsstats.tcl] and [file nsstats.adp] in an administrative page directory.
Configure access control before exposing these pages. OpenACS installations can
use their protected administration directory. The module Makefile installs the
pages and its parameter dictionary; no documentation rendering is required by
an ordinary installation.

[section DIAGNOSTICS]
When the core [cmd ns_stats] command is available, ready shared samples provide
interval rates and timing averages. The utilization page shows sampling age and
interval and permits selecting a live snapshot. History uses SQLite persistence
when configured, or the bounded in-memory sample buffer. Charts break across gaps
and restarts; missing values remain unknown. Sampling and persistence are configured
in the process-wide [const ns/stats] section, independently of this web interface.
Older installations retain the original collectors.

[para]
The parameter reference loads the core dictionary and available installed module
dictionaries. The MCP administration page appears when nsmcp is active; inspection
calls require an explicit administrator action and use the normal protocol checks.

[section CONFIGURATION]
[include include/parameters.man]

[section DOCUMENTATION]
The repository-local [file doc/tcl/config-parameters.tcl] is authoritative for the
parameters below. Generate the committed include with [const {make regen-config-parameters-includes}].
[const {make check-doc}] checks freshness and validates the complete manual.
[const {make build-doc}] creates standalone HTML and nroff documentation.
For the complete web-interface guide, see
[uri https://github.com/naviserver-project/nsstats/blob/main/README.md {the repository README}].
[keywords monitoring statistics configuration ns_stats]
[section {MODULE ADMIN PAGES}]
Modules publish reusable ADPs through the server-scoped nsstats:plugins NSV
array. Each provider key holds a dictionary mapping page IDs to descriptors.
Required fields are label, title, group, scope and an absolute readable adp path.
The optional requires field names a command that must exist. Groups are overview,
memory, background, logs and administration; scopes are global, server, mixed
and source. Page IDs start with a lowercase letter and contain lowercase letters,
digits, dots, underscores or hyphens. Built-in pages cannot be replaced.
[example_begin]
nsv_set nsstats:plugins example [lb]dict create example.status [lb]dict create \
    label Example title {Example status} group administration scope server \
    requires ::example::Service adp /module/lib/status.adp[rb][rb]
[example_end]
Registration can precede the first nsstats request. Discovery uses the current
server registry and omits unavailable or invalid pages. Remove a provider with
nsv_unset nsstats:plugins example. Treat registration as trusted module code,
never as browser input. Pages appear in navigation and retain normal nsstats
access checks before their ADP is evaluated. Header/footer helpers and ordinary
table styles are available. Direct JSON/download responses must leave ADP output
empty, including whitespace. The plugin retains responsibility for POST, CSRF
and application authorization. The nsmcp module owns its MCP ADP and companion
Tcl file in lib; future UI changes deploy with nsmcp alone after this host upgrade.

[manpage_end]
